{
  "//": "tsc --checkJs over the shared platform modules and pure-logic modules (JSDoc types, no build step, nothing emitted). Run: npm run typecheck. `pages` (round 12) = page scripts that declare top-level globals ($, video, mode ...) which collide with other pages: each is checked as its own program with the shared ambient types plus its own types/*.d.ts. `strictNull` (round 12) = gated files that must ALSO pass with strictNullChecks (errors are counted only in those files; the next step is strict for them, then more files). Add a file to `files` once it type-checks cleanly (npm run typecheck:report lists the rest). sw.js is excluded: it runs in a ServiceWorkerGlobalScope, not the DOM lib.",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "commonjs",
    "lib": [
      "ES2022",
      "DOM",
      "DOM.Iterable"
    ],
    "types": [],
    "strict": false,
    "noImplicitThis": true,
    "strictBindCallApply": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "useUnknownInCatchVariables": false,
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
